# Work docs home

Durable documentation, reports, experiment writeups, eval result dumps, and agent memos go under **`~/projects/work-docs`** (repo `nthpaul/work-docs`) — not `/tmp`, not repo `tmp/`, not Desktop/Downloads.

## Where to put things

| Kind | Directory |
|---|---|
| Experiment writeups / one-off analyses | `experiments/<slug>/` |
| Analytics / attribution notes | `analytics/<slug>/` |
| Domain deep-dives (ops memory, cert evals, …) | top-level topic folder, e.g. `neutron-ops-actions-memory/` |
| Raw `/tmp` rescues, logs, tool I/O worth keeping | `scratch/<slug>/` with a short `README.md` |
| Multi-ticket plans | `plans/<slug>/` |

Use a dated or ticket-scoped slug (`neutron-ops-actions-skills-ab`, `tmp-noise-2026-07`). Include a `README.md` that states source, date, and what is/isn't curated.

## Do / Don't

- **Do** write new docs straight into `work-docs` while working.
- **Do** commit + push `work-docs` when the user asks to save or ship docs (same git hygiene as other repos).
- **Don't** leave the only copy in `/tmp`, worktree `tmp/`, or chat-only.
- **Don't** dump secrets (tokens, Infisical exports, raw auth headers). Redact or skip.
- **Don't** put product source code or PR patches here — code stays in the product repo.

Ephemeral compile/test logs that nobody will re-read can stay in `/tmp`. If you might need it next week, put it in `work-docs`.
